  [warning] Comparison with NaN is always true
   ╭─[test.lis:5:11]
 4 │   let x: float64 = 1.0
 5 │   let _ = x != math.NaN()
   ·           ───────┬───────
   ·                  ╰── always true
 6 │ }
   ╰────
  help: Per IEEE 754, NaN compares unequal to every value including itself. Use `math.IsNaN(x)` to test for NaN · code: [lint.nan_comparison]
